# Tale of Einbroch (Taenzerin)  |  Skill 8114  |  Sprache: Mittelhochdeutsch
# Quelle: Suno aligned_lyrics (Tale of Einbroch - Female.mp3), Zeitbasis = Wiedergabestart der WAV
# ms<TAB>original<TAB>english   (english leer = Vocable/Chor -> keine Blase; ~ = Start geschaetzt, Suno-Alignment unsicher)
# [Intro – pickaxe on stone, then anvil answers, pit crew hums]
18822	(Mmmmm… mmm-brrum… mmmmm…)	
18895	(Mmmmm… mmm-brrum… mmmmm…)	
# [Bar 1, Stollen 1 – pit crew, hoarse, hum underneath]
19000	Ez was ein tac als ander tage,	It was a day like any other day,
22899	wir vuoren in bi grawem lieht.	we went down in the grey light.
26610	Diu lampe bran, der hamer sluoc –	The lamp burned, the hammer struck –
30064	und niemen sach, waz obene geschiht.	and no one saw what happened above.
# [Bar 1, Stollen 2 – forge crew, hard, every syllable a hammer]
34007	Ez was ein tac als ander tage,	It was a day like any other day,
38032	diu esse gluot, der zein was heiz.	the forge glowed, the iron was hot.
41702	Do wart der wint so swaer und stille,	Then the wind grew heavy and still,
45479	der rouch gie nider, gel und weiz.	the smoke sank down, yellow and white.
# [Bar 1, Abgesang – both crews together]
48937	Do kam daz weter durch die stat,	Then the poison-weather came through the town,
52939	daz niemen ruoft und niemen bat.	and no one called out, and no one prayed.
56542	Diu tür gie zuo. Der tac wart naht.	The door fell shut. Day turned to night.
# [Chorus – both crews, anvil and pickaxe together]
63772	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
67899	Slahet, daz man ez hoere!	Strike, so that they hear it!
71290	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
75239	Slahet, biz si komen!	Strike, until they come!
# [Bar 2, Stollen 1 – pit crew, growling, then quieter]
80370	Wir sazen tief in unser naht,	We sat deep in our night,
83976	und obene wart ez stiller stunt.	and above it grew ever stiller.
86521	Kein rat, kein wagen, keine stimme –	No wheel, no cart, no voice –
91676	wan ein hamer sluoc. Der was uns kunt.	only a hammer struck. That one we knew.
# [Bar 2, Stollen 2 – forge crew, clipped]
95292	Wir stuonden in dem gelben rouch	We stood in the yellow smoke
99335	und horten unden niht ein wort.	and heard not a word from below.
102979	Do sprach der alte an der esse:	Then the old man at the forge said:
106569	Slahet. Si vindent uns an dem ort.	Strike. They will find us by it.
# [Bar 2, Abgesang – both crews together, slow]
110214	Ein hamer ist ein kleinez lieht,	A hammer is a small light,
114156	doch hoert man in, swa man niht siht.	yet you hear it where you cannot see.
117819	Slac umbe slac: der wec nach hus.	Blow by blow: the way home.
# [Chorus – both crews, anvil and pickaxe together]
124969	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
129096	Slahet, daz man ez hoere!	Strike, so that they hear it!
132527	EINBROCH! (EIN BRUCH!) (EIN SLAC!)	EINBROCH! (A BREAK!) (A STRIKE!)
150949	Slahet, biz si komen!	Strike, until they come!	~
# [Break – only one slow hammer on the anvil, far away, pit crew hums toward it]
157137	(Mmmmmmm… mmmmmmm…)	
157177	(Brrrrum… mmmmm… brrrrum…)	
# [Bar 3, Stollen 1 – pit crew, whispered, then rising]
157280	Wir giengen nach dem slage uf	We climbed up toward the blows
160995	durch weter, daz die brust verbran,	through weather that burned the chest,
164881	und kamen uz bi der esse,	and came out beside the forge,
168710	und ieglicher greif eine hant.	and each one grasped a hand.
# [Bar 3, Stollen 2 – forge crew, low, half-time]
172186	Sit sluoc kein hamer mer umbe golt	Since then no hammer struck for gold
175771	und keiner umbe herren, die niht sehent.	and none for lords who do not see.
178457	Er sluoc umbe die, die unden sint –	It struck for those who are below –
183710	daz si wizzen, wa die lebenden stent.	so they know where the living stand.
